From c5835c70d2cdfd06b63b25649572fe8659464dbb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: netplay <netplay@localhost>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 19:54:36 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 13/42] netplay: SNES core (protocol v2, 12-bit inputs, mailbox
 at 0x3FC00000)

The SNES core is recognised by name. Its mailbox, magic and 12-bit
entry format follow SPEC.md 10.3; HELLO carries a system byte and INPUT
16-bit samples (version 2). NES stays version 1 byte for byte. SNES
settings go into HELLO; WRAM/ARAM must be 00FF or FF; MSU-1, BS-X,
real-time clocks and the competition carts are refused. Recordings
NPR3 with 16-bit samples. The lobby looks for .sfc/.smc and asks the
server for this core's games. Tests: SNES engine tests and NP_SYSTEM=snes
UDP runs, directly and through a server.
